Changes: a Python implementation of the spike-sensitive update is used for
completed inference executions. It is bounded by request-context groups, a
recent empirical p90, expiry, sample counts, and explicit cold fallback. It
does not decay estimates to zero on reads or implement Finagle's endpoint
selection, pending-request accounting, or network retry behavior.
